# .certify/scopes.map — which TEST SCOPES a changed path must run at PUSH.
#
# One line per rule: a path pattern, then the scopes, comma-separated. The
# FIRST matching line wins, so the narrow rules stand above the wide ones. The
# pattern is a shell `case` glob matched against the path from the repo root:
# `*` crosses directories, so `static/*` is everything under static/.
#
# A path that matches NO line REFUSES the push (scripts/ci/scopes.sh exits 3
# and names it). Nothing is waved through and nothing is guessed: a new kind
# of file gets a line here in the commit that adds it.
#
# THE SCOPES (run by scripts/ci/gate.sh, each one alone or together):
#   docs      nothing runs. Prose no test reads.
#   static    gofmt, go vet, go build, node --check. The guard set: cheap,
#             whole-tree, and added to every push that is not docs-only.
#   js        node --test static/js/*_test.mjs
#   unit      every Go test but TestFeatures, under the race detector
#   features  TestFeatures: the Gherkin scenarios, in parallel shards, no -race
#   rigs      the bash rigs under scripts/ci/tests/ (the gate's own tests)
#   image     docker build of the production image, never pushed
#   whole     static, js, unit, features, rigs. RELEASE runs this plus image.
#
# THE SEAM, said honestly: every Go file is one package (package main at the
# repo root), so a product .go change reaches every Go test and the smallest
# sound selection for it is unit + features. The lean lanes are the ones a
# real boundary cuts: prose, the browser scripts' own tests, a scenario or its
# step bindings, the gate's own scripts, the image recipe. A finer cut needs
# packages, not a cleverer map.
#
# A *_steps_test.go change runs features and not unit: go vet (static) still
# compiles every test, and the whole suite at RELEASE covers the rare plain
# test that calls a step helper.

# prose
*.md                        docs
docs/*                      docs
LICENSE                     docs
.env.example                docs

# the gate itself, and the workflows that call it
scripts/*                   static,rigs
.certify/*                  static,rigs
.github/*                   static,rigs
.claude/*                   docs

# the image recipe and the Fly config
Dockerfile                  image
.dockerignore               image,unit
fly.toml                    image
APP_PROFILE.yaml            docs
.gitignore                  unit

# the og-card bake: the baked card has its own Go test, the script nothing else runs
tools/*                     unit

# the baked layers the trip card is drawn on (embedded by social_card.go)
cardlayers/*                unit,features

# the module graph: everything
go.mod                      whole
go.sum                      whole

# browser scripts: their own tests are a real seam
static/js/*_test.mjs        js
static/js/*_harness.mjs     js,features
static/*                    js,unit,features
templates/*                 unit,features

# scenarios and their bindings
features/*                  features
*_steps_test.go             features

# fixtures, the embedded history, and every other Go file
testdata/*                  unit,features
seed/*                      unit,features
*.go                        unit,features
